          "content": "```python\ndef sieve_primes(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Return all prime numbers less than or equal to n using the Sieve of Eratosthenes.\"\"\"\n    if n < 2:\n        return []\n\n    # Assume all numbers are prime initially, then mark known non-primes.\n    is_prime = [True] * (n + 1)\n    is_prime[0] = is_prime[1] = False\n\n    # Only need to mark multiples for factors up to sqrt(n).\n    for number in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if is_prime[number]:\n            # Mark multiples of the current prime as non-prime.\n            for multiple in range(number * number, n + 1, number):\n                is_prime[multiple] = False\n\n    # Collect primes in increasing order.\n    return [number for number in range(2, n + 1) if is_prime[number]]\n```",
